        "metadata": {
            "kira_final": "Done. `/app/convert_masks.py` is written and verified end-to-end on the demo data.\n\n**How it works:**\n1. Loads MobileSAM (`vit_t`) from the given weights path on CPU (or GPU if available) via the official `mobile_sam` package — MobileSAM source is untouched.\n2. Rasterizes every input mask (polyline → `fillPoly`, degenerate/rectangle-only rows → bounding box).\n3. Runs MobileSAM once per mask with a **box prompt** derived from the mask extent, requesting 3 candidate masks; picks the highest-scoring candidate that is a single contiguous component (largest connected component enforced) and does not overlap any previously claimed pixel — guaranteeing no inter-mask overlap and one contiguous region per cell. Falls back to the original mask minus occupied pixels if needed.\n4. Extracts closed polylines with `cv2.findContours`, updates `xmin/xmax/ymin/ymax/coords_x/coords_y` (and sets `type=polyline`), preserving all other columns.\n5. Saves to `<output_path>/<csv basename>`.\n\n**Verification on demo set:** all 48 masks output as closed polylines, zero overlap between masks, every mask single-contiguous, ~28% image coverage. Runtime ≈10 s on CPU (~5 masks/s). I also installed the missing deps in the container (`torch` CPU build, `timm`, `pandas`, `tqdm`, `opencv-python-headless`) and downloaded weights to `/app/mobile_sam.pt` for testing.",
            "session_id": "tb-c4eb3dc565"
        }
